[34m==>[0m Running scenario 'pick_and_place' against zone 'cell_b' on DDS domain 43
[33mwarn[0m Seed 20260824 reaches 'gz sim --seed' only — this run is not reproducible.
[33mwarn[0m   That seeds gz::math::Rand: sensor noise and transport RNG.
[33mwarn[0m   It does NOT seed the physics solver.
[33mwarn[0m   Planning: what is PROVEN is that one move_group answers an identical request
[33mwarn[0m   identically within one process (cite_skills' planning-pipeline launch test).
[33mwarn[0m   That is repeatability, not scenario determinism, and it holds only where Pilz
[33mwarn[0m   answered; the OMPL fallback is unseeded and unseedable (ADR-0006). Grep this
[33mwarn[0m   run's log for 'planner fallback:' to see which motions took it, and for
[33mwarn[0m   'planner fallback declined:' for the ones that refused a substitute.
